{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"abdominal-grieving-nandu","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context (operator escalation R3/C11.3, 2026-08-12)\n\nThe code-review gate RUNS its Pass-2 verify judge (gates/code-review.yaml verify step; usage-log rows for op=code-review-verify confirm live calls), but 0 of ~1,400 recorded code_review_result_v2 sidecar findings carry a `verification` block ({binary, severity_attributes}) — while all 22,503 plan-review findings do. The per-finding binary answers and severity attributes exist in-run and are dropped before persistence (`code_review/sidecar.py::build_payload` passes findings through `_with_norm_ids` only; the plan-review sidecar's `_slim` deliberately persists `verification` for offline calibration and the code path has no analog). Consequence: no offline corpus exists to calibrate or migrate code-review's impact model (the ordinal-migration plan is blocked on this), and — the operator's larger concern — NOTHING ERRORS OR WARNS when an expected recording is absent, so the gap survived ~1,400 reviews unnoticed.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Persist each code-review finding's `verification` block in the sidecar payload (mirror plan-review's `_slim` field-selection rationale; schema-tolerant readers unaffected).\n2. Error signal for missing metrics: at sidecar build time, when the verdict's findings lack verification blocks while the verify step reports it ran, log a WARNING naming the count and record `coverage.metrics.verification_recorded=false` so the absence is measurable; a parity/unit test pins that a verify-step finding carries the block.\n3. Backstop test asserting the sidecar payload for a verified finding round-trips {binary, severity_attributes}.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A code-review run's sidecar findings carry `verification.binary` and `verification.severity_attributes` when the verify step ran. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"code_review and sidecar\"` passes with a new round-trip test.\n- [ ] When findings lack verification while verify ran, the sidecar records `verification_recorded=false` in its metrics and logs a warning. Verify: covered in the same test module.\n- [ ] Existing sidecar readers are unaffected (schema-tolerant). Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"sidecar\"` passes.","id":"884d-ece3-c961-4959","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"code-review sidecar drops Pass-2 verification blocks and nothing signals the gap"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786505032214149001,"uuid":"0b8507d2-4b59-4bda-a583-247fa3ea31ff"}